From: MilkFlint4 <noreply@milkflint4.local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-usxgmii: skip link-up reconfig for in-band USXGMII

Re-running pcs_config from pcs_link_up drops the carrier of a link that
just came up. On the GL-BE14000 10G WAN (in-band USXGMII to the C45 PHY)
that flaps the port every one to two seconds for as long as it is up.

Keep the RX re-tune for 10GBASE-R and fixed-mode trunks; skip it when
the interface is USXGMII (in-band AN already settled).

Based on the OpenWrt / community fix reported against Flint 4 builds
(openwrt#26690 and related forum reports).

Signed-off-by: MilkFlint4 <noreply@milkflint4.local>
---
--- /tmp/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c.orig	2026-11-21 08:16:23.818398204 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-usxgmii.c	2026-11-21 08:16:23.838398193 +0000
@@ -325,9 +325,13 @@
 				    phy_interface_t interface,
 				    int speed, int duplex)
 {
-	/* Reconfiguring USXGMII to ensure the quality of the RX signal
-	 * after the line side link up.
+	/* Reconfigure after link-up for modes that need an RX re-tune.
+	 * In-band USXGMII already finished AN; reconfiging it drops the
+	 * carrier and flaps forever on boards such as the GL-BE14000.
 	 */
+	if (interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII)
+		return;
+
 	mtk_usxgmii_pcs_config(pcs, neg_mode, interface, NULL, false);
 }
 
